 atmosphere. With no air to scatter sunlight, the sky stays black even at noon — and the stars never twinkle."}},{"id":"21e95ea4-da2f-420a-830b-a585bc884c05","createdAt":1786894182510,"transform":{"position":[-16,3.774758283725532e-15,-17],"rotation":[0,0.9,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":-16,"z":-17,"rotY":0.9,"eyebrow":"The flag","title":"It is not waving","body":"No air means no wind. A horizontal rod along the top hem holds the flag out flat. The ripples are just creases from being rolled up."}},{"id":"695c8ef6-69e2-4370-86b2-77e881e55f61","createdAt":1786894182512,"transform":{"position":[26,5.773159728050814e-15,-26],"rotation":[0,-0.9,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":26,"z":-26,"rotY":-0.9,"eyebrow":"Lunar Roving Vehicle","title":"The Moon buggy","body":"About 10 feet long — twice your height. Wheels of woven piano wire, because rubber tyres would crack in vacuum. Top speed: 8 mph."}},{"id":"eeb76006-95ad-46b4-9fa7-591b75b23f53","createdAt":1786894182513,"transform":{"position":[-17,4.884981308350689e-15,-22],"rotation":[0,0.6,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":-17,"z":-22,"rotY":0.6,"eyebrow":"Lunar Module","title":"Two ships in one","body":"Only the top half flew home. The gold foil is Kapton, wrapped on to keep the temperature steady between +250°F in sun and -280°F in shade."}},{"id":"1d8e9488-8a98-4148-93b5-794ff2292d34","createdAt":1786894182514,"transform":{"position":[13,1.7763568394002505e-15,-8],"rotation":[0,-0.4,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":13,"z":-8,"rotY":-0.4,"eyebrow":"Footprints","title":"They are still there","body":"No wind, no rain, no running water. The prints left in 1969 could stay sharp for millions of years — only micrometeorites slowly erase them."}},{"id":"0c022431-732a-43ad-960c-a41a879fc0e2","createdAt":1786894182515,"transform":{"position":[-33,-0.0008953021058402122,-26],"rotation":[0,0.9,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":-33,"z":-26,"rotY":0.9,"eyebrow":"ALSEP","title":"Experiments still running","body":"The mirror panel here reflects laser beams straight back to Earth. Scientists still fire at it, and have measured the Moon drifting 1.5 inches farther away each year."}},{"id":"3de9314e-af5c-4241-bc06-7d1ebf20f6d1","createdAt":1786894182517,"transform":{"position":[-38,-0.03727917392145397,28],"rotation":[0,-0.4,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":-38,"z":28,"rotY":-0.4,"eyebrow":"What comes next","title":"Living here","body":"A lunar day lasts about 29.5 Earth days — two weeks of sun, then two weeks of night. Any real base has to store power for all of it."}},{"id":"18649ffd-078f-45ec-aaa4-f3449c85962c","createdAt":1786894182518,"transform":{"position":[7,5.500000000000005,-24],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f5f5f5"},{"id":"d8cceaab-cc03-450b-926f-7b45b5819144","createdAt":1786894182519,"transform":{"position":[-9,5.500000000000006,-27],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#3d8bf2"},{"id":"f0a82f87-ecf3-4bea-a99f-96870795a2d4","createdAt":1786894182520,"transform":{"position":[-30,5.999999999999998,6],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#3d8bf2"}]}